   910	/**Function*************************************************************
   911	
   912	  Synopsis    [Returns 1 if an stmap area-sensitive mode should reject a cut.]
   913	
   914	  Description [The area-sensitive guards are evaluated after matching the
   915	  candidate cut because their hypotheses need the candidate's actual mapper
   916	  area. In stmap6 exact-area recovery, a wide high-fanout cut is rejected only
   917	  when the existing match has slack and the candidate does not save at least
   918	  half an inverter area. In stmap7, the area-saving override additionally
   919	  requires more than two inverter delays of slack and excludes the highest
   920	  fanout-risk bucket. In stmap8, the override is further rejected when the
   921	  candidate match worsens mapper arrival by more than one quarter of an
   922	  inverter delay. In stmap9, middle-slack candidates can recover area only
   923	  when they are outside the highest fanout bucket, do not worsen mapper
   924	  arrival, and save at least one inverter area. In stmap10, that middle-slack
   925	  relief also requires the mapper node to be no deeper than level 96. In
   926	  stmap11, that depth window is tightened to level 64. In stmap12, the same
   927	  tight-depth relief is allowed only in the lower moderate fanout bucket. In
   928	  stmap13, the same decision path also records exact-area guard statistics. In
   929	  stmap14, the lower-moderate middle-slack relief must save two inverter areas
   930	  instead of one. In stmap15, one-inverter relief is restored only after the
   931	  mapper observes a high lower-moderate/middle-slack profile. In stmap16, the
   932	  same behavior also reports each admitted relief choice. In stmap17, the
   933	  adaptive one-inverter relief threshold also requires a material mapper-arrival
   934	  improvement; arrival-neutral choices keep the stricter two-inverter fallback.
   935	  In stmap18, the same decisions are preserved while near-miss rejected
   936	  middle-slack candidates are logged. In stmap19, pre-profile one-inverter
   937	  relief is seeded only by candidates with the same material arrival gain. In
   938	  stmap20, the pre-profile seed is further limited to shallow nodes. In
   939	  stmap21, deeper pre-profile seeds are allowed only with a much larger mapper
   940	  arrival gain. In stmap22, the same deep-seed path is relaxed to a moderate
   941	  mapper-arrival gain. In stmap23, moderate deep seeds also need near-critical
   942	  existing mapper slack. In stmap24, the moderate deep slack gate is tightened
   943	  to the lower edge of the critical slack window. In stmap25, the stmap24 rule
   944	  is kept, and one moderate deep seed from the next slack band is admitted for
   945	  ablation. In stmap26, the first such moderate seed is skipped and only the
   946	  second qualifying seed is admitted. In stmap27, moderate deep candidates in
   947	  the next slack band are admitted unless they match the high-reference,
   948	  low-slack, stronger-moderate signature isolated by stmap26. In stmap28, that
   949	  hard blocker is replaced by a soft area-margin penalty on high-reference
   950	  moderate seeds whose slack and arrival-gain ratios resemble load-risky
   951	  choices. In stmap29, the high-reference penalty is made continuous over the
   952	  same seed band. In stmap30, the same load-risk surface is extended to
   953	  high-reference strong deep seeds with a smaller continuous penalty. In
   954	  stmap31, the strong-seed gain slope is damped to probe the penalty threshold.
   955	  In stmap32, a cut-leaf load proxy adds a candidate-cut fanout-shape term to
   956	  the strong-seed penalty.]
   957	
   958	  SideEffects []
   959	
   960	  SeeAlso     []
   961	
   962	***********************************************************************/
   963	static int Map_MatchSkipAreaSensitiveFanout( Map_Man_t * p, Map_Node_t * pNode, Map_Cut_t * pCut, int fPhase, Map_Match_t * pMatchBest, Map_Match_t * pMatch )
